{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And he will lift up.</b> As though he lifts up a banner to every nation until it comes to make war against Israel, and likewise \"and he will whistle for him.\"" "<b>Swiftly he will come.</b> In a swift time he will come, or it is an adjective of the coming [participle], and this is the correct [interpretation]."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:57.535392386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}